This tests the amd64 link-editor's handling of Initial Executable TLS sequences.

The original C source files are in orig/ but unused, since we need to avoid
any changes to the compiler influencing our tests.

Further we have an object style2-with-badness.elf built from
orig/style2-with-badness.s using "GNU assembler (GNU Binutils) 2.32" which is
willing to assemble the bad instruction under test where modern assemblers are
not.

